What this migration does, in plain English:
  - Drops the legacy cold-path schema:
      cagg_vehicle_daily / cagg_climate_hourly / cagg_battery_daily
        (CAGGs over the legacy signal_log carried over from
        000147_continuous_aggregates),
      cagg_signal_hourly
        (CAGG over signal_observations from 000142_baseline_typed § 26),
      signal_log         (legacy hypertable from 000040 +
                          000145_signal_history_to_signal_log;
                          old columns: created_at / vehicle_id /
                          signal / value_num / value_str / value_bool /
                          value_jsonb),
      signal_observations + signal_catalog
        (legacy cold-path tall hypertable + registry from
        000142_baseline_typed § 08-09).
    Drop order is enforced (CAGGs before hypertable; observations
    before catalog because of the FK).
  - Recreates `signal_log` per the prompt-mandated schema:
      vehicle_id BIGINT NOT NULL,
      ts         TIMESTAMPTZ NOT NULL,
      field      TEXT NOT NULL,
      value_kind SMALLINT NOT NULL  (matches protomodel.ValueKind range),
      str_value  TEXT,
      bool_value BOOLEAN,
      int_value  BIGINT,
      float_value DOUBLE PRECISION,
      time_value TIMESTAMPTZ,
      PRIMARY KEY (vehicle_id, ts, field)  -- exactly-once cold path.
  - Promotes to a 7-day-chunk hypertable with if_not_exists=>TRUE.
  - Creates the prompt-mandated indexes:
      signal_log_vehicle_field_ts (vehicle_id, field, ts DESC)
      signal_log_field_ts          (field, ts DESC)
  - Applies a TABLE COMMENT and per-column COMMENTs documenting the
    layered live-state contract and the typed-column / value_kind
    mapping for every protomodel.ValueKind.
  - down.sql drops the new signal_log table (forward-only rollback —
    no legacy schema to restore).
  - Honesty covenants 1-10: unchanged.

