  All five INSERTs returned `INSERT 0 1`.

  SELECT count(*), array_agg(field ORDER BY ts) FROM signal_log;
   ->  5 | {BatteryLevel,Gear,BMSState,DriveRail,LastUpdate}

PK collision test (composite PK gives exactly-once semantics):
  INSERT INTO signal_log (vehicle_id, ts, field, value_kind, float_value)
    VALUES (1, '2026-05-04 02:00:00+00', 'BatteryLevel', 6, 0.42);
   ->  INSERT 0 1
  INSERT INTO signal_log (vehicle_id, ts, field, value_kind, float_value)
    VALUES (1, '2026-05-04 02:00:00+00', 'BatteryLevel', 6, 0.99);
   ->  ERROR:  duplicate key value violates unique constraint
       "1_1_signal_log_pkey"
       DETAIL:  Key (vehicle_id, ts, field)=(1, 2026-05-04 02:00:00+00,
       BatteryLevel) already exists.
  (The chunk-level PK index name `1_1_signal_log_pkey` is the
  TimescaleDB internal name for the per-chunk unique index — Timescale
  installs one per chunk, all backed by the parent PK.)

